0..71 Comment "// Bounded naturals as they should read, and what refuses each program."
72..74 Comment "//"
75..150 Comment "// `Finite(n)` holds the naturals below `n`. A case on one binds each arm\'s"
151..226 Comment "// index equation. It solves an equation with a variable side and prunes an"
227..303 Comment "// arm whose ends are apart. It prunes no match of no arms. The model source"
304..374 Comment "// `injective-index` declares `Finite` and holds `toNat` and `lookup`."
375..377 Comment "//"
378..449 Comment "// The checker refuses each declaration below by the name its attribute"
450..528 Comment "// states. Each turns to `checks` as its rung lands, and the source then moves"
529..550 Comment "// to the model root."
551..553 Comment "//"
554..616 Comment "// - owes: #3484 — the empty match at an indexed family, for"
617..633 Comment "//   `absurdFin`"
634..689 Comment "// - see: #3481 — the spike that wrote these programs"
691..727 Comment "// The naturals the bounds count in."
